      "shortDescription": "FRIEDRICH Schwingtechnik develops vibration drives for industrial conveying, screening and process equipment. Its official range includes electric vibration motors, flange-mounted and explosion-protected variants, unbalance exciters and VIMARC vibration motors.",
      "fullDescription": [
        "FRIEDRICH Schwingtechnik GmbH is a German vibration-technology manufacturer based in Haan. The company's official product material focuses on vibration motors and unbalance exciters used to generate controlled oscillation in industrial machinery.",
        "The documented range includes standard and special electric vibration motors, flange-mounted units, ATEX and IECEx variants for potentially explosive environments, VIMARC motor configurations and F16/F17 unbalance exciters. The exciters are designed to drive vibratory conveyors, screens and other vibration systems with high payloads or flow rates, while the manufacturer's download centre provides brochures, operating manuals, certificates, declarations and spare-parts documentation for the main motor and exciter families."
      ],
